# Base URL for FlyWeather-Soaring's published products (manifest.json +
# wstar/*.webp,*.json) - see that repo's docs/PRODUCT_CONTRACT.md. A
# separate, independently-hosted static file set, not part of this app's
# own build.
#
# Leaving this unset/empty is a fully supported state: the RASP toggle
# still appears, but turning it on shows "unavailable" rather than a
# layer - the rest of the app is completely unaffected.
#
# Development options:
#   - Point at a local copy: run `flyweather-soaring generate` in the
#     FlyWeather-Soaring repo, copy its products/v1/ into this repo's
#     public/soaring-dev/, then: VITE_SOARING_BASE_URL=/soaring-dev
#   - Point at FlyWeather-Soaring's own GitHub Pages once published:
#     VITE_SOARING_BASE_URL=https://utskottet.github.io/FlyWeather-Soaring
#     (no /v1 suffix - upload-pages-artifact publishes products/v1's
#     contents at that repo's Pages root, not under a /v1 path)
#
# VITE_SOARING_BASE_URL=

# Visitor counting (optional, off by default - see src/app/analytics.ts).
# Leaving these unset is a fully supported state: nothing is injected and
# no third-party request is made.
#
# Both supported providers are cookieless and store no personal data, so
# neither requires a consent banner. The token is public in either case
# (it is visible in the page source of every site using them), so it is a
# repository *variable*, not a secret.
#
#   Cloudflare Web Analytics - create a site in the Cloudflare dashboard,
#   copy its beacon token:
#     VITE_ANALYTICS_PROVIDER=cloudflare
#     VITE_ANALYTICS_TOKEN=<32-character beacon token>
#
#   GoatCounter - register a site code at goatcounter.com (the token is
#   the code itself, e.g. `startvind`, or a full endpoint URL if the site
#   lives on a custom GoatCounter domain):
#     VITE_ANALYTICS_PROVIDER=goatcounter
#     VITE_ANALYTICS_TOKEN=startvind
#
# VITE_ANALYTICS_PROVIDER=
# VITE_ANALYTICS_TOKEN=
